"""
patch-effect-bodies-2026-09-11.py

Applies the "Revised Prompts" batch (30 effects) to
lib/v1/portraits/portraits-bodies.ts.

Source: Revised_Prompts.zip, uploaded 2026-09-11, one .prompt.txt per
effect. Body/avoid split was inferred per file (a trailing "**Avoid:**",
"AVOID:", or plain "Avoid ..." paragraph, separated from the rest by a
blank line, becomes the avoid field; everything before it is the body).
Files with no such trailing paragraph get avoid: null.

TWO DELIBERATE EDITS ON TOP OF THE RAW ZIP CONTENT, confirmed with Rich
before this script was generated:
  - art_deco:    "his/him" pronouns (8 instances) neutralized to
                 "the subject" / "their" / "them"
  - art_nouveau: "his" pronouns (2 instances) neutralized the same way
  Both files mixed "his" and "her" in the same body -- a leftover from
  editing against one reference photo (same fault class as the Persian
  Court pets port, 20 August). Every other effect below ships VERBATIM
  from its .prompt.txt; no other wording was changed.

Anchors are matched against portraits-bodies.ts AS READ BY THIS SCRIPT AT
RUN TIME -- never from a project-knowledge copy or from memory. If the
live file has drifted (an id missing, appearing more than once, or not
matching the expected `id: / body: / avoid:` shape), that id is SKIPPED
and reported; nothing else about that id is guessed at.

NOTHING IS OVERWRITTEN WITHOUT AN ARCHIVE FIRST, same law as
Install-File.ps1 / FILE-PLACEMENT.md. Before any write, the whole
pre-patch file is copied to ArchiveRoot (default H:\\minramas, override
with --archive-root) under a name that has never been used before --
<name>_001.ts, then _002 on a second run, and so on; an existing
archived copy is never touched. If the archive drive is not there, this
script REFUSES to write, same as Install-File does -- an edit with
nowhere safe to put the original is an overwrite wearing a different
name. This script never calls os.remove, shutil.rmtree, or truncates
anything; the only write is the final open(path, "w").

Nothing partial is written: either every matched id updates cleanly, the
original is archived, and the new file is verified on disk -- or nothing
about the target file changes at all.

Usage:
  python patch-effect-bodies-2026-09-11.py <path-to-portraits-bodies.ts>
      Dry run (default). Reports what would change. Touches nothing --
      no archive copy, no write.

  python patch-effect-bodies-2026-09-11.py <path-to-portraits-bodies.ts> --apply
      Archives the current file, writes the patched version, then
      re-reads it and verifies every changed id's new body text is
      actually present before exiting 0.

  python patch-effect-bodies-2026-09-11.py <path> --apply --archive-root D:\\other-archive
      Use a different archive root (defaults to H:\\minramas, matching
      Install-File.ps1's own default).
"""

